tegra: ORIN-GLASSINK — blevels closes the AA pass's one false-PASS path (PANEL_BG is on the ramp)

A host run of this file's own `lad_classify` — extracted verbatim, not replicated —
found that `video::PANEL_BG` (0x001E1E1E) is a GREY and therefore sits ON the
black-to-light-grey ramp, so the segment test calls it a blend. A content box holding
some paper and a lot of desktop would have cleared the blend supermajority and read
as GLYPHS-AA-ON-GLASS: the rung would have PASSED on the desktop showing through.

What separates a flat fill from anti-aliased text is not the colour but the number of
COVERAGE LEVELS: a fill has exactly one, glyph edges sampled across many strokes have
several. The census now carries `blevels=0|1|2+`, the AA verdicts require `2+`, and a
one-level supermajority gets its own verdict INK-FLAT-FILL rather than being folded
into the scatter bucket - so `ink1=0x001e1e1e blevels=1 -> INK-FLAT-FILL` names the
desktop by value on the wire. Two locals and one compare per blend sample.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
